[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643646211","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113784#issuecomment-3643646211","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113784","id":3643646211,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZLaED","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-11T20:22:44Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T20:23:34Z","body":"I think the removal of 'first_time_kinematic' is a breaking change for Godot Physics. If you e.g. spawn an object at the origin, make it kinematic and then call `set_transform(some large distance from the origin)`, the body will in 1 frame sweep from the origin to this new transform, imparting a large velocity on objects that it collides with. Before this PR, the body would have teleported and not caused any issues.\r\n\r\nI don't disagree with this solution, but I've made another API suggestion at https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113712#issuecomment-3643592772 (which is also a breaking API change).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643646211/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643855226","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113784#issuecomment-3643855226","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113784","id":3643855226,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZMNF6","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-11T21:28:02Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T21:42:28Z","body":"@jrouwe If we are to make an API change I am more in favour of removing / deprecating `first_time_kinematic` and doing it the Jolt way (automatically teleport while not in a space) and changing the documentation to make the behaviour of setting the transform of kinematic bodies clear because it honestly makes things more confusing. Really all that would have to be added is that setting the transform while inside the space sweeps, whereas doing it outside the space teleports.\r\n\r\nCases where `first_time_kinematic` can be confusing:\r\n- Not setting an initial transform will cause a teleport instead of a sweep on the first transformation even if not intended\r\n- Setting the transform more than once before entering a space will sweep from the first set transform to the last when entering a space\r\n- Leaving a space does not reset `first_time_kinematic`, meaning this doesn't work if a body is being reused\r\n\r\nA user would not know any of this without looking at the code as I don't believe this is mentioned anywhere. Keeping this behaviour is something that could be behind a project setting if truly needed. From what I recall there is already plumbing so that projects that upgrade from previous versions could automatically set this setting, while new ones dont.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643855226/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644516087","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113784#issuecomment-3644516087","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113784","id":3644516087,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZOub3","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-12T01:31:27Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T01:31:27Z","body":"I've added a project setting that is disabled by default but enabled when upgrading an existing project which keeps the now-deprecated `first_time_kinematic` behaviour. This pr doesn't break compat now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644516087/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3769865590","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113784#issuecomment-3769865590","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113784","id":3769865590,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gs5V2","user":{"login":"patrykkalinowski","id":7796424,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3OTY0MjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7796424?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski","html_url":"https://github.com/patrykkalinowski","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-19T19:43:43Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T19:43:43Z","body":"Great fix. I have problem with kinematic RigidBodies not moving at all when coded with small movements per frame, this PR fixes the issue. I run physics between 144 and 180Hz, so delta is very very small.\r\n\r\nThis code doesn't do anything on master, while on PR branch rotates correctly\r\n```\r\nextends RigidBody3D\r\n\r\nfunc _physics_process(delta: float) -> void:\r\n\ttransform = transform.rotated_local(Vector3.UP, deg_to_rad(0.01 * delta))\r\n\tforce_update_transform()\r\n\tflush_kinematic_transform()\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3769865590/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]